  ;; ============================================================
  ;; PIN ASSIGNMENTS (documented as text annotation)
  ;; ============================================================
  (text "STM32H743VIT6 PIN ASSIGNMENTS (Rev 1.2 - SPI-based architecture):\n\n=== COMMUNICATION PERIPHERALS ===\nSPI1/LoRa SX1276: PA5(SCK), PA6(MISO), PB5(MOSI), PA4(NSS_LORA), PC13(DIO0_IRQ), PC2(RST)\nSPI2/WiFi ATWINC1500: PB13(SCK), PB14(MISO), PB15(MOSI), PB12(NSS_WIFI), PB1(CHIP_EN), PC0(RST_N), PD10(IRQ_N)\nSPI3/Flash W25Q64JV: PB3(SCK), PB4(MISO), PB2(MOSI), PA15(NSS_FLASH) [REMAPPED from PC10-12 for SDMMC1]\nSPI4/Ethernet W5500: PE2(SCK), PE5(MISO), PE6(MOSI), PE4(NSS_ETH), PE3(RST_N), PB0(INT_N)\nUSART1/Debug Console: PA9(TX), PA10(RX) -> J12 header (115200 baud)\nUART4/GSM SIM7600: PA0(TX), PC11(RX), PC3(PWR_KEY), PD11(STATUS)\nUART7/BLE RN4870: PE8(TX), PE7(RX), PD12(RST_N_BLE), PD13(STATUS_BLE)\nFDCAN1: PD0(RX), PD1(TX)\nUSART2/RS485: PD5(TX), PD6(RX), PD4(DE/RE)\n\n=== STORAGE ===\nSDMMC1 (4-bit): PC8(D0), PC9(D1), PC10(D2), PC11(D3), PC12(CLK), PD2(CMD)\nI2C1/EEPROM: PB6(SCL), PB7(SDA)\n\n=== ANALOG / DIGITAL I/O ===\nADC1: PA0-PA3 (4 channels, 16-bit)\nDI GPIO: PD3, PD7, PE0, PE1, PE9-PE12 (8x digital inputs via optocouplers)\nDO GPIO: PE13-PE15, PD14 (4x relay driver outputs)\n\n=== SYSTEM ===\nUSB_OTG_FS: PA11(DM), PA12(DP)\nSWD: PA13(SWDIO), PA14(SWCLK)\nBOOT0: Dedicated pin, jumper J13 (GND=flash boot, 3V3=DFU mode), R16 10k pull-down default\nNRST: Reset with RC filter + TPS3823 WDT output\nHSE: PH0(OSC_IN), PH1(OSC_OUT) - 25MHz\nLSE: PC14(OSC32_IN), PC15(OSC32_OUT) - 32.768kHz\nWDT_KICK: PB8 (TPS3823 WDI input)\n\n=== PROGRAMMING INTERFACES ===\nJ10: 10-pin ARM SWD header (Samtec FTSH-105-01-L-DV-K, 1.27mm pitch)\nJ11: USB-C connector (USB_OTG_FS for DFU programming)\nJ12: UART debug console header (4-pin 2.54mm: VCC/TX/RX/GND, USART1 PA9/PA10)\nJ13: BOOT0 select jumper (3-pin: GND-BOOT0-3V3, default=flash boot)\nJ14: Tag-Connect TC2050-IDC pads (production programming, same SWD signals as J10)\n\nNOTE: RMII pins freed (PA1,PA2,PA7,PB11,PC1,PC4,PC5) by using W5500 SPI Ethernet\nNOTE: SPI3 remapped from PC10-12 to PB3/PB4/PB2 to free PC8-12 for SDMMC1 4-bit SD card"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "MCU-TEXT-0001")
  )
)
